<div class="footnotes">
  <table>
    <tr>
      <td class="num">(1)</td>
      <td>3 Tx Simultaneous operation in AWR1843 and AWR2243 is supported only with 1V LDO bypass and PA LDO disable mode. In this mode 1V supply needs to be fed on the VOUT PA pin. Please refer to the respective datasheets for more information.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="num">(2)</td>
      <td>AWR294x supports a real only receiver.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="num">(3)</td>
      <td>Developed for Functional Safety applications, the AWR294x device is targeted to support hardware integrity up to ASIL-B. For other devices, refer to the respective Datasheets.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="num">(4)</td>
      <td>Device security features including Secure Boot and Customer Programmable Keys are applicable to select part number variants as indicated by the Device Type identifier in the <span class="link">Section 3</span>, Device Information table.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="num">(5)</td>
      <td>In AWR294x, Main-Subsystem Processing core is changed from Arm CR4F in AWR1843 to Arm CR5F.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="num">(6)</td>
      <td>The DSP processing core in AWR294x is upgraded from C67x in AWR1843 to C66x.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="num">(7)</td>
      <td>The hardware accelerator in AWR294x is upgraded to HWA2.1 with additional features as compared to AWR1843. AWR2944LC has M4 core in HWA</td>
